  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A higher-up task reaches Shang Xin Ci on Shang Liang Mountain about the contest for Fur blessed land. The blessed land holds Fur true inheritance and is exposed by the qi tide; because of its remote location it belongs to no Southern Border super force, so the super clans fight over it. Righteous path Gu Immortals agree to send Gu Masters to decide the winner and bar Gu Immortal interference.",
      "chapters": [
        2126
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shang_xin_ci",
        "loc_shang_liang_mountain",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "sys_righteous_path",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Secret information on the owner, Fur Immortal, says she dual cultivates wood path and transformation path without an excellent method, so conflicting dao marks keep her battle strength low and leave her bullied among Gu Immortals. Shang Xin Ci judges that none of the super forces are interested in such a true inheritance, and that the blessed land’s location is the real value: if Shang clan wins it as an exclave, the territory can be sold to nearby super forces as a bridgehead or front-line site in the opening great era. She treats the contest as Shang clan’s most urgent priority and plans to send Feng Tian Yu as head of the Gu Master party.",
      "chapters": [
        2126
      ],
